DESCRIPTION:Main dish and fruits or veggies\nNo grains\, legumes\, hummus
 \, \nNo sugar or soy\nNo processed foods with preservatives.\nNo zucchin
 i please. \nThings that work:\nPlease cook with coconut oil\, bacon fat\
 , or organic butter.\nDishes can be dressed with olive oil\, but please 
 don't cook with it. \nChicken\, salmon\, white fish\, eggs\, and grass-f
 ed beef are all good options.\nLentils and all fruits and vegetables are
  ok. \nWhite potatoes and sweet potatoes are ok.\nOrganic milk products 
 and organic peanut products work as well.\nPlease use organic produce. \
 nPlease text Anne before you deliver the food.\nPlease just bring a main
  dish and either a fruit or vegetable. \nAnne's pantry is regularly stoc
 ked with fresh fruits and vegetables and lentil pasta that she can add t
 o the meals we bring. You are also welcome to come and prepare a dish in
  her kitchen with Anne using the fresh fruits and vegetables that she ha
 s in her home. \n\nAnne said that you could google 'Paleo Main Dishes wi
 th no grain' or Paleo Side Dishes with no grain' and most recipes will b
 e within Caylor's dietary restrictions. Anne is happy to answer any ques
 tions you may have about recipes or ingredients. They have some of the m
 ore unsual spices or items already in their home that they can add after
  you bring the meal.
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20160211T170000
DTSTAMP:20160211T203949Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20160211T120000
LAST-MODIFIED:20160211T203948Z
LOCATION:1622 Hoover Ave\nSouth Bend Indiana 46615\n574-850-2880
SEQUENCE:8
